{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggqhicFDPimvhwpFWnWw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dq = 1750 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 618 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 2494 cm⁻¹. I got Dq and B from the three spin-allowed bands and C from the spin-forbidden band.\n\n**Dq.** For octahedral d³, the lowest spin-allowed band is ⁴A₂g → ⁴T₂g, and it equals Δ = 10Dq exactly. So 10Dq = 17 500 cm⁻¹ and Dq = 1750 cm⁻¹.\n\n**B.** The other two spin-allowed bands, ⁴A₂g → ⁴T₁g(F) and ⁴A₂g → ⁴T₁g(P), come from diagonalising the ⁴T₁g matrix. Their sum is ν₂ + ν₃ = 15B + 3Δ.\n- ν₂ + ν₃ = 23 860 + 37 910 = 61 770 cm⁻¹.\n- 3Δ = 52 500 cm⁻¹, so 15B = 9270 cm⁻¹ and B = 618 cm⁻¹.\n\nAs a check, the splitting ν₃ − ν₂ should equal √(225B² + Δ² − 18BΔ). That gives 14 054 cm⁻¹, against 14 050 cm⁻¹ observed.\n\n**C.** The lowest spin-forbidden band is ⁴A₂g → ²Eg, observed at 12 090 cm⁻¹. This level depends on C, so I computed the full d³ term energies at Dq = 1750 and B = 618 with the term-table tool.\n- At C = 2831, ²Eg is at 13 116 cm⁻¹.\n- At C = 2490, ²Eg is at 12 077 cm⁻¹.\n- The slope is about 3.05 cm⁻¹ per cm⁻¹ of C, so matching 12 090 cm⁻¹ gives C ≈ 2494 cm⁻¹.\n\nThe two spin-allowed bands the tool computes at Dq = 1750 and B = 618 are 23 858 and 37 912 cm⁻¹, matching the observed 23 860 and 37 910 cm⁻¹. The ratio C/B is about 4.0.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1750, \"B\": 618, \"C\": 2494, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq from ν1=10Dq, B from ν2+ν3=15B+30Dq, C from fitting the ²Eg energy at 12090 cm⁻¹.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2200,"cache_read_input_tokens":10873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2200,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae8